{"type":"text","text":"Done. All three HUD values found by blind differential search, proven by writes, recorded, and promoted to the mapping file.\n\n## Results — SMB World 1-1 HUD RAM\n\n| HUD value | Address(es) | Encoding |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Coin count** (displayed `xNN`) | **`$07ED`–`$07EE`** | BCD, one digit per byte: tens `$07ED`, ones `$07EE` |\n| **Level timer** (TIME) | **`$07F8`–`$07FA`** | BCD, one digit per byte: hundreds `$07F8`, tens `$07F9`, ones `$07FA` |\n| **Score** (MARIO) | **`$07DD`–`$07E2`** | BCD, one digit per byte, MSB at `$07DD`; RAM holds score÷10, the HUD appends a hard-wired `0` ones digit |\n\nBonus, found in the same runs: **`$075E`** = per-level binary coin counter (0–99, 1-UP at 100) — *not* the displayed value.\n\n### How each was found and proven\n\n**Coins.** Snapshot → grabbed the first 1-1 `?`-block coin (HUD `x00`→`x01`, score 000000→000200) → `diff increased` gave 68 hits; a second coin (`x01`→`x02`, score 000200→000400) with `from: d1` narrowed to 63. Last round quoted `$07EE 1→2` and `$075E 1→2`. Proof: writing `[8,8]` to `$07ED/$07EE` alone did **not** move the screen (the status bar only redraws on a coin event), so I collected a real coin — screenshot showed **`x89`** and read-back was `$07ED=8, $07EE=9` (the tens digit showing 8, not the old 0, proves both bytes). After the run reached game over, `$075E` read 0 while the HUD still showed `x89`, showing the BCD digits are the persistent count.\n\n**Timer.** Two no-input windows (375→356→340) narrowed `changed` survivors from 53 to 26; last round: `$07F9 5→3`, `$07FA 6→1` (hundreds `$07F8` only rolls at the digit boundary). Proof: `write_memory $07F8-$07FA = [9,9,9]` → HUD showed **TIME 999**, then ticked itself to **996** (screenshot); the written hundreds/tens 9s held.\n\n**Score.** The two coins left `$07E1` as an `increased` survivor, and read-back of `$07DD`–`$07E2` was `[0,0,0,0,4,0]`. Extent proof per the skill: wrote `[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]` to `$07DC`–`$07E3`, forced a redraw with a coin (+200). The HUD read **`2345870`** — digits from `$07DD`–`$07E2` appeared in order (2,3,4,5,8,7) with `$07E1` incremented 6→8 by the +200, while the `$07DC` `1` and the `$07E3` `8` never appeared. Nametable row 3 confirms columns 2–8 = `2 3 4 5 8 7 0`. That fixes the range at exactly `$07DD`–`$07E2`.\n\nAll four entries recorded with `source: \"differential search\"` and `promote_mappings` was called (mapping file now has 12 addresses). I also restored the save state taken before the write-proofs, so the emulator is back in 1-1 as it was."}
